{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Testing release. Requires ReaImGui 0.10. See EULA.md before use.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaRoll\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaRoll is a MIDI piano roll for REAPER by Davvo. {\b 0.7.2-test} expands note editing, chords, controller editing, glides and MPE while keeping the familiar piano roll and bottom tools. This is a release for user testing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab REAPER\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ReaImGui 0.10 or newer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Optional: js_ReaScriptAPI (install through ReaPack) enables modifier + wheel actions over an unfocused ReaRoll panel on Windows and macOS. Without it, click ReaRoll first to use modified scrolling and zooming.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install or update\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab In REAPER, choose {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Import {\f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/davvolinni-ui/ReaRoll/main/index.xml}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Synchronize packages, then install or update {\b ReaRoll}. If the testing version is not offered, enable pre-releases for this package or select {\b 0.7.2-test} in the package browser.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Close an already running ReaRoll instance, then run {\b ReaRoll - MIDI piano roll} from the Action List. The action file remains {\f1 ReaRoll/ReaRoll.lua}.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Existing preferences are retained. The package also installs {\b ReaRoll - Reset Window} for recovering a hidden or off-screen window.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 What's new in 0.7.2-test\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fix Shape Apply staying greyed out for valid single-item previews; keep the window open if committing fails.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Use ReaImGui's modifier state for drawing, selection and keyboard shortcuts.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Limit physical modifier polling to wheel actions over an unfocused ReaRoll panel on Windows and macOS, with js_ReaScriptAPI installed. The Windows behavior has been user-tested; live macOS verification is pending.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 What's new in 0.7.1-test\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fix Shape velocity selection across editable MIDI channels and multiple items.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Keep selected notes selected during Shape previews, Apply and Cancel, and clear old errors after a successful preview.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Start the empty piano roll at project zero instead of the previous item's scroll position.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 What's new in 0.7.0-test\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Overlap-driven mono glides and independent MPE chord glides.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Automatic MPE member-channel allocation for drawing, per-note Pitch/Pressure/Timbre editing, live curve previews and multi-note expression editing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Multiple-item editing through the same piano roll, with the original note tools and navigation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Scale-aware chord palettes, click or drag chord placement, pitch-locked note painting and tool context menus.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Expanded controller lanes, controller editing tools, and controller/sustain following for supported note moves and copies.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Compact toolbar controls, optional mouse tooltips, stronger key-color selection feedback and recalled floating-window placement.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fixes for drawing, resizing, take lifetime handling and glide persistence at item boundaries.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Getting started\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Notes:} click empty grid to draw; drag while inserting to set the end. Drag a note body to move it or either edge to resize. Input presets can change these gestures.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Chords:} choose a scale, open the chord palette, and drag a chord into the roll. Drag while placing to choose its duration.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Glide:} enable the glide icon, then overlap successive notes. The overlap sets the transition timing. For independent chord voices, enable MPE in ReaRoll and use an MPE-capable instrument.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b MPE:} match the instrument's zone, member-channel count and pitch-bend range. New MPE notes receive channels automatically. The expression icon opens Pitch, Pressure and Timbre editing; right-drag selects curve points. Changing ReaRoll's MPE switch changes its editing mode and does not remove MIDI already written.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Multiple items:} use the overlapping-items icon to choose the editing scope and drawing destination.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Settings:} use the three-dot menu for mouse tooltips, appearance, shortcuts and mouse modifiers. {\b Quick guide} explains the editing gestures.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaRoll's pitch-bend range must match the instrument. It does not automatically configure a plug-in. Ordinary MIDI pitch bends affect their whole channel; independent simultaneous bends use MPE member channels.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Input presets\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Open {\b the three-dot menu > Shortcuts and mouse modifiers} to choose {\b ReaRoll Default}, {\b REAPER}, {\b FL Studio}, or {\b Ableton Live}. Applying a preset replaces keyboard and note-grid mouse bindings; individual edits become {\b Custom}. Existing saved shortcuts are preserved until you choose a preset.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Presets adapt familiar Windows controls to supported ReaRoll actions. See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "docs/INPUT_PRESETS.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
input preset details
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Feedback and license\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Report issues in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://forum.cockos.com/showthread.php?t=311021"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaRoll forum thread
}}}
. Include the exact steps, expected and actual results, active tool, REAPER/ReaImGui versions, and instrument settings when relevant. A small reproducible MIDI example is helpful.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaRoll is distributed under its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ReaRoll/EULA.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
End User License Agreement
}}}
. Public access to this repository does not grant an open-source license. See also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ReaRoll/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
third-party notices
}}}
.\par}
}
